{"authored" [{"question" "q-8359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x-y}{x}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x-y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{x}-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & +\\frac{y}{x}=\\frac{2x}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & +{{\\frac{1}{x}}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y={{2}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1546f0e9b1bf06bff40e7bfc86b9a5dacb385ae508daadb1ff3ece564edf5238" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nNote that the option\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{x}y={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nis already is written in standard form with  $P(x)=-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{x}$ and $Q(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Since the equation is written in standard form, we conclude that it is a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations cannot be written in the standard form, and therefore they are not first-order linear ODEs." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1546f0e9b1bf06bff40e7bfc86b9a5dacb385ae508daadb1ff3ece564edf5238" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103554" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103554" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{x}^{2}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103554" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)={x}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103554" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{x}y={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103554" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{e}^{xy}=x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103554" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}-{x}^{3}=\\sqrt{1+y}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-331738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are inhomogeneous?\n\n- ${y}^{′}+4xy=2$\n- ${y}^{′}+4xy=0$\n- ${y}^{′}+4xy=y$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-331738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nA first-order linear differential equation is inhomogeneous if it is not homogeneous, i.e., if it can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $Q$ is not identical to zero.\n\nTo determine which equations are inhomogeneous, we examine each one in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4xy=2.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is written in the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)$ where $Q(x)=2$ is not identically zero. Therefore, this equation is inhomogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4xy=0.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is already zero, so the equation directly matches the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4xy=y.\n$$\n\nWe collect the $y$-terms on the left side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+4xy & =y \\\\ {y}^{′}+4xy-y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+(4x-1)y & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-331738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1546f0e9b1bf06bff40e7bfc86b9a5dacb385ae508daadb1ff3ece564edf5238" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-331738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-331738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/1403693