ifferential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-331738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-331605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are inhomogeneous?\n\n- ${y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=3x$\n- ${y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=0$\n- ${y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=y$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-331605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nA first-order linear differential equation is inhomogeneous if it is not homogeneous, i.e., if it can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $Q$ is not identical to zero.\n\nTo determine which equations are inhomogeneous, we examine each one in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=3x.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is written in the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)$ where $Q(x)=3x$ is not identically zero. Therefore, this equation is inhomogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation has the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=y.\n$$\n\nWe collect the $y$-terms on the left side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y & =y \\\\ {y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y-y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+({x}^{2}-1)y & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our equation can be written in the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0,$ the equation is homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-331605" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1546f0e9b1bf06bff40e7bfc86b9a5dacb385ae508daadb1ff3ece564edf5238" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-331605" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-331605" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "