a_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/state.json" "file_sha256" "3f3c6c02e6b9fad31c7093c3f11718755eab26d12a28fe5a1fe5029aee35bf13" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}\n+\ny\\sin x\n-\n\\cos x\n=0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/example-6599.json" "file_sha256" "b162cdee3aec5248d3227203ea4910cdd414fb8fc7caea5034609eb2d140516f" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6599" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}\n+\nP(x)y\n=\nQ(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=\\sin x$ and $Q(x) = \\cos x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/example-6599.json" "file_sha256" "b162cdee3aec5248d3227203ea4910cdd414fb8fc7caea5034609eb2d140516f" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6600" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine whether the following equation is a first-order linear ODE:\n\n$$\nx^2\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}\n+\n\\sin(2x)y\n=\ne^x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/example-6600.json" "file_sha256" "2504be715e059feba8a322f1766c943a8b43e34ff362a7cfd2f13a988eed8683" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6600" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We attempt to write the equation in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}\n+\nP(x)y\n=\nQ(x) \\,.\n$$\n\nDividing the equation through by $x^2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)y & ={e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{{x}^{2}}y & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that this equation is now in standard form with $P(x) = \\dfrac{\\sin{2x}}{x^2}$ and $Q(x) = \\dfrac{e^x}{x^2}.$\n\nBecause the equation can be written in standard form, we conclude that it is a first-order linear ODE." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/example-6600.json" "file_sha256" "2504be715e059feba8a322f1766c943a8b43e34ff362a7cfd2f13a988eed8683" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-21813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are inhomogeneous?\n\n- $y' + x^3 y = 0$\n\n- $y' + x^3 y = x^4$\n\n- $y' + x^3 y = y$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/example-21813.json" "file_sha256" "7b3e7d259253ad7a897ab7e74e3014bf36bd16e73b0f2c86b9a702c37d402503" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-21813" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\ny' + P(x)y = 0.\n$$\n\nA first-order linear differential equation is inhomogeneous if it is not homogeneous, i.e., if it can be written as\n\n$$\ny' + P(x)y = Q(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $Q$ is not identical to zero.\n\nTo determine which equations are inhomogeneous, we examine each one in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\ny' + x^3 y = 0.\n$$\n\nNotice that this has the form $y' + P(x)y = 0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\ny' + x^3 y = x^4.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is written in the form $y' + P(x)y = Q(x)$ where $Q(x) = x^4$ is not identically zero. Therefore, this equation is inhomogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\ny' + x^3 y = y.\n$$\n\nWe collect the $y$-terms on the left side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y & =y \\\\ {y}^{′}+{x}^{3}y-y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+({x}^{3}-1)y & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our equation can be written in the form $y' + P(x)y = 0,$ the equation is homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/example-21813.json" "file_sha256" "7b3e7d259253ad7a897ab7e74e3014bf36bd16e73b0f2c86b9a702c37d402503" "basis" 1250 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036933/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/state.json" "file_sha256" "605789ec174e771c3c5366888c5c8e14f92b2f4eef81c4e70bf6fe52f4a04372" "basis" 1623 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nNote that the option\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)y=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nis already is written in standard form with  $P(x)=-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Since the equation is written in standard form, we conclude that it is a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations cannot be written in the standard form, and therefore they are not first-order linear ODEs." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/state.json" "file_sha256" "605789ec174e771c3c5366888c5c8e14f92b2f4eef81c4e70bf6fe52f4a04372" "basis" 1623 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103551" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "eb4d28ad52ee2323cc5eba3288092cabe973f18909117f96787114c62ba4296e" "basis" 1623 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/state.json" "file_sha256" "605789ec174e771c3c5366888c5c8e14f92b2f4eef81c4e70bf6fe52f4a04372" "basis" 1623 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy={x}^{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/state.json" "file_sha256" "605789ec174e771c3c5366888c5c8e14f92b2f4eef81c4e70bf6fe52f4a04372" "basis" 1623 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)=x-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/state.json" "file_sha256" "605789ec174e771c3c5366888c5c8e14f92b2f4eef81c4e70bf6fe52f4a04372" "basis" 1623 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)y=\\frac{1}{x}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/state.json" "file_sha256" "605789ec174e771c3c5366888c5c8e14f92b2f4eef81c4e70bf6fe52f4a04372" "basis" 1623 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-{x}^{3}y=\\frac{x}{1+y}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/state.json" "file_sha256" "605789ec174e771c3c5366888c5c8e14f92b2f4eef81c4e70bf6fe52f4a04372" "basis" 1623 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}+{x}^{2}y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/state.json" "file_sha256" "605789ec174e771c3c5366888c5c8e14f92b2f4eef81c4e70bf6fe52f4a04372" "basis" 1623 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-103551" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)y=\\frac{1}{x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/state.json" "file_sha256" "605789ec174e771c3c5366888c5c8e14f92b2f4eef81c4e70bf6fe52f4a04372" "basis" 1623 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043781/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-79699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n5{y}^{2}-y{e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y,\\,y\\ne 0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-y{e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ -y{e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5{y}^{2}-y & =0 \\\\ -y({e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y+1) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y+1 & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y+1) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y{e}^{x}+{e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,+{{(-5{e}^{x})}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{-{e}^{x}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5{e}^{x}y & =-{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=-5{e}^{x}$ and $Q(x)=-{e}^{x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f03af7a1550f93a859827dcb9678a9d79dd79007f48b332b2f0b1f95fdbe735"} {"question" "q-79699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5xy=-{e}^{-x}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,+5y=-{e}^{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,+5{e}^{-x}y={e}^{-x}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,-5{e}^{x}y=-{e}^{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,-5{e}^{x}y=x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,-5{e}^{x}y=-{e}^{x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x+y}{x}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x+y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}(\\frac{x+y}{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x(x+y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}+xy \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,+{{(-x)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{{x}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=-x$ and $Q(x)={x}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f03af7a1550f93a859827dcb9678a9d79dd79007f48b332b2f0b1f95fdbe735"} {"question" "q-79697" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79697" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+xy=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(1+x)y=0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy=2x"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy={x}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y=-{x}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79697" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy={x}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-8359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x-y}{x}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-8359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x-y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{x}-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & +\\frac{y}{x}=\\frac{2x}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & +{{\\frac{1}{x}}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y={{2}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-8359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f03af7a1550f93a859827dcb9678a9d79dd79007f48b332b2f0b1f95fdbe735"} {"question" "q-8359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-8359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y-2=0"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y=2"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{x}y+2"] ["math" "x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=2x"] ["math" "y=2x-x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-8359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y=2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-16400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-16400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =1-4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ 2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-16400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f03af7a1550f93a859827dcb9678a9d79dd79007f48b332b2f0b1f95fdbe735"} {"question" "q-16400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-16400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=1+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)y=1+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}=(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-16400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)y=\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-16396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\ny\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y={y}^{2}x\\,,\\,y\\ne 0\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-16396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y & ={y}^{2}x \\\\ y\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y-{y}^{2}x & =0 \\\\ y(\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}-yx) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}-yx & =0 \\\\ \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\,{{(-x)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{-{x}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{dy}{dx}-xy & =-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=-x$ and $Q(x)=-{x}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-16396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f03af7a1550f93a859827dcb9678a9d79dd79007f48b332b2f0b1f95fdbe735"} {"question" "q-16396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-16396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{x}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{1-{x}^{2}}{1+{x}^{2}}y=1"] ["math" "\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y=x"] ["math" "\\frac{dy}{dx}-xy=-{x}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=-2x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-16396" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{dy}{dx}-xy=-{x}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79753" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79753" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nNote that the option\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(\\sqrt{x})y=x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\n$$\n\nis already is written in standard form with  $P(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ and $Q(x)=x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$ Since the equation is written in standard form, we conclude that it is a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations cannot be written in the standard form, and therefore they are not first-order linear ODEs." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79753" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f03af7a1550f93a859827dcb9678a9d79dd79007f48b332b2f0b1f95fdbe735"} {"question" "q-79753" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79753" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(\\sqrt{x})y=x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\sqrt{(xy)}=x+1"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy=\\frac{1}{y-1}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y={y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-79753" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(\\sqrt{x})y=x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-103567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-103567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nLet's attempt to write $\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{2x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y}$ in the standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{2x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{2x}y & =y\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{2x}y & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is in standard form with  $P(x)=-x{e}^{2x}$ and $Q(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Since the equation is written in standard form, we conclude that it is a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations cannot be written in the standard form, and therefore they are not first-order linear ODEs." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-103567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f03af7a1550f93a859827dcb9678a9d79dd79007f48b332b2f0b1f95fdbe735"} {"question" "q-103567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-103567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x{e}^{2x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{2x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{y}={x}^{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y{e}^{2x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y}"] ["math" "y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{y}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-103567" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{2x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071102/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b3cf5ecd35dce5dc5b1457a60886b46030397801921bb369c7af1dcd10b9d9"} {"question" "q-8349" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "